a 10-year-equivalent humidity ageing test must not exceed 10%.\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"candidate_specs.md identifies Radiator-R2 as the porous radiator with a hydrophobic treatment. This is the specified humidity-resistant candidate; untreated porous R1 is rejected on this hard requirement, while lower-index solid R3 fails separation.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Radiator thickness between 1 and 6 cm.\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"Recommended thickness is 3.5 cm, within the allowed 1--6 cm interval.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Achieve the best possible pion/kaon separation at 10 GeV/c.\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"Among options satisfying the ageing and separation constraints, the R2 thickness scan showed the best performance at 3.5 cm. Tested R2 averages were lower at 2.0 cm (~3.74 sigma), 3.0 cm (~3.71 sigma), 3.25 cm (~3.69 sigma), 3.75 cm (~3.69 sigma), and 4.0 cm (~3.69 sigma); R3 never reached 3.5 sigma; R1 was excluded by the humidity-ageing risk.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Finish by submitting one recommended radiator and thickness.\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"Submitted one recommendation: Radiator-R2, 3.5 cm.\"}]}", "call_id": "call_f777fc34898d45f58c721b1cf57f9a7c", "name": "submit_recommendation", "type": "function_call", "id": "fc_0542b542997b5137006b02cfca80c887d09954f8951bdebbb3", "async_": null, "caller": null, "namespace": null, "status": "completed"}]}
